She's a reader.

254
00:13:13,836 --> 00:13:15,504
Sees into the
truth of things.

255
00:13:15,587 --> 00:13:18,632
Might see trouble before it's coming.
Which is of use to me.

256
00:13:18,716 --> 00:13:21,176
And that's your guiding star, isn't it?
What's of use.

257
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:22,594
(RUMBLING)

258
00:13:22,678 --> 00:13:25,764
Honestly, Doctor, I think we may
really crash this time anyway.

259
00:13:25,848 --> 00:13:26,890
(CLICKING)

260
00:13:26,974 --> 00:13:28,475
Do you understand what
I have gone through

261
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:30,019
to keep River away
from the Alliance?

262
00:13:30,102 --> 00:13:32,646
I do, and it's a fact we
here have been courteous

263
00:13:32,730 --> 00:13:34,273
enough to keep
to our own selves.

264
00:13:34,356 --> 00:13:35,482
Are you
threatening to...

265
00:13:35,566 --> 00:13:37,484
I look out for
me and mine.

266
00:13:38,193 --> 00:13:41,447
That don't include you
less I conjure it does.

267
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:45,075
You stuck a thorn in the Alliance's paw.
That tickles me a bit.

268
00:13:45,159 --> 00:13:47,536
But it also means I got to step
twice as fast to avoid them

269
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:50,080
and that means turning
down plenty of jobs.

270
00:13:50,164 --> 00:13:51,540
Even honest ones.

271
00:13:51,957 --> 00:13:54,168
Put this crew together
with the promise of work,

272
00:13:54,251 --> 00:13:56,503
which the Alliance makes
harder every year.

273
00:13:56,587 --> 00:13:58,797
Come a day there won't be
room for naughty men like us

274
00:13:58,881 --> 00:14:00,424
to slip about at all.

275
00:14:00,591 --> 00:14:03,677
This job goes south, there
well may not be another.

276
00:14:04,303 --> 00:14:06,972
So here is us,
on the raggedy edge.

277
00:14:07,056 --> 00:14:08,474
(METAL CLANKING)

278
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:11,685
Don't push me,
and I won't push you.

279
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:14,396
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

280
00:14:26,492 --> 00:14:29,912
Zoe, Wash gonna straighten this
boat out before we get flattened?

281
00:14:29,995 --> 00:14:33,540
ZOE: Like a downy feather, sir.
No one flies like my mister.

282
00:14:33,791 --> 00:14:35,793
(ENGINE GRINDING)

283
00:14:36,627 --> 00:14:38,796
(MAL AND ZOE CHATTERING)

284
00:14:42,758 --> 00:14:43,801
SIMON: River.

285
00:14:44,218 --> 00:14:48,013
I know. We're
going for a ride.

286
00:14:51,642 --> 00:14:53,727
(ENGINE REVVING)

287
00:15:00,609 --> 00:15:02,152
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

288
00:15:07,408 --> 00:15:09,451
Hey, little one.

289
00:15:10,828 --> 00:15:12,996
Understand your
part in all this?

290
00:15:15,332 --> 00:15:16,417
Do you?

291
00:15:18,168 --> 00:15:19,962
This is what I do,
darling.

292
00:15:23,632 --> 00:15:25,008
This is what I do.

293
00:15:27,594 --> 00:15:29,012
MAL: Let's move, people.

294
00:15:30,305 --> 00:15:32,724
Quit fiddling. Want the boat
running smooth when we get back.

295
00:15:32,808 --> 00:15:34,059
Have faith, Captain.

296
00:15:34,143 --> 00:15:35,477
Not today.

297
00:15:36,437 --> 00:15:38,355
Pair of clips
in the rear hatch.

298
00:15:39,606 --> 00:15:42,192
We should hit town right
during Sunday worship.

299
00:15:42,276 --> 00:15:43,610
Won't be any crowds.

300
00:15:43,694 --> 00:15:45,946
If Fanty and Mingo are
right about the payroll,

301
00:15:46,029 --> 00:15:48,073
this could look to be
a sunny day for us.

302
00:15:48,157 --> 00:15:50,075
SIMON: River, stay
behind the others.

303
00:15:50,159 --> 00:15:53,203
If there's fighting, drop
to the floor or run away.

304
00:15:54,204 --> 00:15:56,206
It's okay to leave
them to die.

305
00:15:56,540 --> 00:16:00,043
Doctor, I'm taking your sister
under my protection here.

306
00:16:00,878 --> 00:16:02,588
If anything happens to
her, anything at all,

307
00:16:02,671 --> 00:16:05,549
I swear to you, I will
get very choked up.

308
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:07,634
Honestly.
There could be tears.

309
00:16:16,226 --> 00:16:20,439
Don't mind the Captain none, Simon.
I know he'll look out for her.

310
00:16:21,106 --> 00:16:23,317
They'll be back
before you can spit.

311
00:16:25,986 --> 00:16:28,447
Well, not that you spit.

312
00:16:34,411 --> 00:16:37,164
JAYNE: What are we hoping to find
here that equals the worth of a turd?

313
00:16:37,247 --> 00:16:40,042
MAL: Security payroll. Alliance
don't have the manpower

314
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:42,711
to "enforce the peace"
on every outer-rim planet.

315
00:16:42,794 --> 00:16:45,756
They hire out to the private firms,
who will not work for credit.

316
00:16:45,839 --> 00:16:49,510
They get paid in cashy money,
which, once a month, rests here.

317
00:16:49,593 --> 00:16:51,678
Don't that lead back to
the Alliance, anyhow?

318
00:16:51,762 --> 00:16:54,598
No private firm would ever report
the theft of their own payroll.

319
00:16:54,681 --> 00:16:57,851
They'd appear weak, might
lose their contract.

320
00:16:57,935 --> 00:17:02,022
Yeah, we're as ghosts in this.
Won't but rattle the floor.

321
00:17:02,105 --> 00:17:04,691
Shiny. Let's be bad guys.

322
00:17:05,901 --> 00:17:08,320
Hands and knees and heads bowed down!
Everybody, down!

323
00:17:08,403 --> 00:17:09,780
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

324
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:12,449
(GRUNTING)

325
00:17:18,622 --> 00:17:20,666
Looks like this
is the place.

326
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:24,461
You all wanna be looking very
intently at your own belly buttons.

327
00:17:24,586 --> 00:17:27,798
I see a head start to rise,
violence is going to ensue.

328
00:17:29,258 --> 00:17:30,884
Probably guessed we mean
to be thieving here,

329
00:17:30,968 --> 00:17:33,136
but what we're after
is not yours.

330
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:35,889
So let's have
no undue fussing.

331
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:37,975
She's locked up.

332
00:17:52,614 --> 00:17:54,366
(PEOPLE MURMURING)

333
00:18:23,562 --> 00:18:24,646
(GUN COCKS)

334
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:27,190
Do you know what the
definition of a hero is?

335
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:30,110
Someone who gets
other people killed.

336
00:18:30,402 --> 00:18:32,154
You can look
it up later.

337
00:18:35,365 --> 00:18:37,326
Big happy family.

338
00:18:42,706 --> 00:18:43,790
<i>(BEEPS)</i>

339
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:50,213
At last. We can retire and
give up this life of crime.

340
00:18:54,134 --> 00:18:55,969
(METAL RATTLING)

341
00:18:56,762 --> 00:18:57,763
Hey!

342
00:18:59,431 --> 00:19:02,267
You all are Browncoats, eh?
Fought for independence?

343
00:19:02,351 --> 00:19:04,394
Petty thieving ain't
exactly soldiers' work.

344
00:19:04,478 --> 00:19:08,774
War's long done. We're all
just folk now. Listen up!

345
00:19:09,483 --> 00:19:11,151
We are coming down
to empty that vault!

346
00:19:11,234 --> 00:19:14,154
GUARD: You have to give me
your authorization password!

347
00:19:15,072 --> 00:19:16,573
(FIRING)

348
00:19:18,241 --> 00:19:19,284
GUARD: Okay.

349
00:19:33,173 --> 00:19:35,550
I'm telling you I heard it.
Repeater.

350
00:19:36,009 --> 00:19:39,888
Did sound somewhat like gun blast.
Maybe you ought run tell Lawman.

351
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,098
(SCREAMING)

352
00:19:42,683 --> 00:19:45,352
What the hell is up?
You all right?

353
00:19:46,144 --> 00:19:47,813
What's going on?

354
00:19:49,356 --> 00:19:50,524
Reavers.

355
00:19:51,608 --> 00:19:53,360
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

356
00:19:57,239 --> 00:20:00,867
The leg is good. It'll bleed plenty
and we avoid any necessary organs.

357
00:20:00,951 --> 00:20:02,285
I was thinking
more of a graze.

358
00:20:02,369 --> 00:20:04,329
No, you don't want it to
look like you just gave up.

359
00:20:04,413 --> 00:20:05,455
No, I get that.

360
00:20:05,539 --> 00:20:06,915
JAYNE: Mal!

361
00:20:06,998 --> 00:20:09,251
Every heist, he's got to
start yelling my name.

362
00:20:09,334 --> 00:20:12,212
Mal! Reavers!

363
00:20:12,546 --> 00:20:15,173
The girl's pitching a fit. They're
here or they're coming soon.

364
00:20:15,257 --> 00:20:16,633
Get on the Mule.

365
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:19,511
Does that lock from the inside?
Yes.

366
00:20:19,594 --> 00:20:22,055
Get everyone upstairs. You get
them down here and you seal it.

367
00:20:22,139 --> 00:20:24,433
As long as you got air, you
don't open up, you understand?

368
00:20:24,516 --> 00:20:25,559
But...

369
00:20:25,642 --> 00:20:27,894
Get them inside
the vault!

370
00:20:28,145 --> 00:20:29,896
You see them?

371
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:31,106
Zoe, take the wheel!

372
00:20:31,189 --> 00:20:32,566
JAYNE: Anybody see them?

373
00:20:34,317 --> 00:20:35,986
(ENGINE REVVING)

374
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,240
Take me with you!

375
00:20:40,323 --> 00:20:41,992
Get back in the vault
with the others.

376
00:20:42,075 --> 00:20:43,285
I can't stay here!
Please!

377
00:20:43,368 --> 00:20:44,995
It's too many.
Move ahead.

378
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:46,496
Please!

379
00:20:49,458 --> 00:20:50,584
Please!

380
00:20:54,087 --> 00:20:56,423
(SCREAMING)

381
00:21:00,719 --> 00:21:02,304
(ENGINE REVVING)

382
00:21:03,805 --> 00:21:05,515
(SCREAMING)

383
00:21:10,353 --> 00:21:12,063
(GRUNTING)

384
00:21:13,732 --> 00:21:14,816
(ROARS)

385
00:21:17,986 --> 00:21:19,196
(FIRING)

386
00:21:21,072 --> 00:21:23,575
Faster! Faster! Faster
would be better!

387
00:21:32,542 --> 00:21:34,211
How come they ain't
blowing us out the air?

388
00:21:34,294 --> 00:21:37,172
They wanna run us down.
The up-close kill.

389
00:21:38,757 --> 00:21:40,967
They want us alive
when they eat us.

390
00:21:41,426 --> 00:21:45,305
Boy, sure would be nice if we had
some grenades, don't you think?

391
00:21:45,388 --> 00:21:46,640
(GUN FIRING)

392
00:21:46,932 --> 00:21:48,975
Wash, baby,
can you hear me?

393
00:21:49,059 --> 00:21:50,101
We're moments from air.

394
00:21:50,185 --> 00:21:51,228
You got somebody behind you?

395
00:21:51,311 --> 00:21:52,479
Reavers.

396
00:21:53,230 --> 00:21:54,314
(MURMURING)

397
00:21:54,773 --> 00:21:55,816
Kaylee!

398
00:21:55,899 --> 00:21:56,983
<i>Heat her up.
We got Reavers.</i>

399
00:21:57,067 --> 00:21:58,068
(GASPS)

400
00:22:01,738 --> 00:22:03,406
We're not gonna
get to you in time.

401
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:04,825
Keep moving, honey.

402
00:22:04,908 --> 00:22:06,493
We're coming to you.

403
00:22:09,704 --> 00:22:10,914
(FIRING)

404
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,001
JAYNE: Where's my clips?

405
00:22:15,085 --> 00:22:16,211
Rear hatch.

406
00:22:16,586 --> 00:22:17,879
(SCREAMING)

407
00:22:24,636 --> 00:22:26,930
(YELLING)

408
00:22:27,013 --> 00:22:28,139
Jayne!

409
00:22:28,306 --> 00:22:30,392
(YELLING)

410
00:22:31,810 --> 00:22:33,186
I won't get ate!

411
00:22:34,479 --> 00:22:38,942
You shoot me if they take me!
Well, don't shoot me first!

412
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,069
(GRUNTING)

413
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:54,791
(GRUNTING)

414
00:22:57,752 --> 00:22:59,713
Get some distance
on them.

415
00:22:59,796 --> 00:23:02,632
You come to the flats, I
want you to swing round.

416
00:23:02,966 --> 00:23:04,885
We're gonna try
a Barn Swallow.

417
00:23:04,968 --> 00:23:06,928
<i>Simon! Open her up!</i>

418
00:23:12,017 --> 00:23:13,476
MAL: They're closing on us!

419
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,770
Those rocks,
give them a taste.

420
00:23:31,369 --> 00:23:33,747
<i>WASH: Okay, baby,
we talked this through.</i>

421
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,376
Talking ain't doing.

422
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:40,003
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

423
00:23:40,879 --> 00:23:42,589
(WHOOSHING)

424
00:24:15,330 --> 00:24:17,082
(GRUNTING)

425
00:24:17,165 --> 00:24:18,833
(GROANING)

426
00:24:18,917 --> 00:24:20,543
River?

427
00:24:20,627 --> 00:24:22,379
I swallowed a bug.

428
00:24:26,841 --> 00:24:28,843
Are you okay?

429
00:24:28,927 --> 00:24:30,345
(INDIGNANTLY) Is he okay?

430
00:24:43,650 --> 00:24:46,027
<i>WASH: We all here?
What's going on?</i>

431
00:24:46,319 --> 00:24:47,612
Hello?

432
00:24:50,115 --> 00:24:51,408
No casualties.

433
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:52,742
Anybody following?

434
00:24:52,826 --> 00:24:54,160
<i>WASH: Nice flying, baby.</i>

435
00:24:54,244 --> 00:24:56,705
That's a negative.
Clean getaway.

436
00:24:57,080 --> 00:25:01,376
Set course for Beaumonde. First
thing, I want this body...

437
00:25:01,459 --> 00:25:02,502
KAYLEE: Simon!

438
00:25:03,503 --> 00:25:04,963
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

439
00:25:05,505 --> 00:25:07,257
You son of a whore.
I'm a hair's breadth

440
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:08,675
from riddling you
with holes, Doctor.

441
00:25:08,758 --> 00:25:10,844
One simple job!
She'll be fine!

442
00:25:10,927 --> 00:25:12,178
She is fine!

443
00:25:12,262 --> 00:25:14,347
Except for being still crazy,
she's a picture of health!

444
00:25:14,431 --> 00:25:18,184
Wasn't for River, we'd probably
be left there. She felt them coming.

445
00:25:18,351 --> 00:25:20,437
Never again.
Do you understand me?

446
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:23,314
Seems I remember a talk about
you giving orders on my boat.

447
00:25:23,398 --> 00:25:24,941
Well, we're
off your boat.

448
00:25:25,025 --> 00:25:27,444
Just as soon as River gets
her share of the bounty.

449
00:25:27,527 --> 00:25:28,862
Let's not do
anything hasty...

450
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:30,321
No, shiny!

451
00:25:30,613 --> 00:25:32,157
We'll be on Beaumonde
in 10 hours' time,

452
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:35,118
you can pick up your earnings
and be on your merry.

453
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:38,246
Meantime, you
do your job.

454
00:25:39,122 --> 00:25:40,707
Patch up my crew.

455
00:25:43,043 --> 00:25:44,669
He didn't lie down.

456
00:25:46,463 --> 00:25:48,131
They never lie down.

457
00:25:57,098 --> 00:25:59,267
ZOE: No, I think things will
glide a deal smoother for us

458
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:01,269
without River and
Simon on board,

459
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:03,271
but how long do you
think they'll last?

460
00:26:03,354 --> 00:26:04,397
Doc made his call.

461
00:26:04,481 --> 00:26:05,482
Yeah.

462
00:26:05,565 --> 00:26:07,400
They's as babes in a basket
when we took them in.

463
00:26:07,484 --> 00:26:09,277
We sheltered
them plenty.

464
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:12,697
Man has to cut loose, learn
to stand on his own.

465
00:26:14,574 --> 00:26:16,367
Like that man
back in town?

466
00:26:19,329 --> 00:26:20,747
I had to shoot him.

467
00:26:20,830 --> 00:26:22,749
What the Reavers would've done
to him before they killed him...

468
00:26:22,832 --> 00:26:25,251
I know. That was
a piece of mercy.

469
00:26:26,252 --> 00:26:29,214
But before that, him begging
us to bring him along.

470
00:26:30,381 --> 00:26:33,259
We couldn't take the weight.
Would've slowed us down.

471
00:26:33,343 --> 00:26:34,761
You know that
for certain?

472
00:26:34,844 --> 00:26:36,679
Mule won't run
with five.

473
00:26:37,347 --> 00:26:41,059
I should've dumped the girl?
Or you? Or Jayne?

474
00:26:41,226 --> 00:26:42,519
Oh, Jayne...

475
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:44,938
You could've
tossed the payload.

476
00:26:45,021 --> 00:26:46,314
Tossed the...

477
00:26:47,524 --> 00:26:51,236
Zoe, I got bits falling off my ship,
I got a crew ain't been paid,

478
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:54,280
and,oh,yeah,a powerful need
to eat sometime this month.

479
00:26:54,739 --> 00:26:56,449
We tell Fanty and Mingo
we skunked the job,

480
00:26:56,533 --> 00:26:58,535
what do think
they'll do to us?

481
00:27:00,370 --> 00:27:02,288
We're close to
gone out here.

482
00:27:03,456 --> 00:27:05,875
We get a job,
we got to make good.

483
00:27:06,459 --> 00:27:09,087
Sir, I don't disagree
on any particular point.

484
00:27:10,839 --> 00:27:12,006
It's just,

485
00:27:15,218 --> 00:27:18,429
in the time of war, we would've
never left a man stranded.

486
00:27:19,848 --> 00:27:21,558
Maybe that's
why we lost.

487
00:27:30,942 --> 00:27:32,610
That was close.

488
00:27:34,946 --> 00:27:36,322
JAYNE: I do not get it.

489
00:27:37,198 --> 00:27:38,992
How's a guy
get so wrong?

490
00:27:39,075 --> 00:27:42,579
Cutting on his own face,
raping and murdering.

491
00:27:45,456 --> 00:27:47,458
I'll kill a man
in a fair fight,

492
00:27:48,251 --> 00:27:50,753
or if I think he's gonna
start a fair fight,

493
00:27:51,629 --> 00:27:55,175
or if he bothers me,
or if there's a woman,

494
00:27:55,592 --> 00:28:00,430
or if I'm getting paid. Mostly
only when I'm getting paid.

495
00:28:01,598 --> 00:28:04,309
These Reavers,
the last 10 years,

496
00:28:04,392 --> 00:28:07,228
they show up like the
bogeyman from stories.

497
00:28:08,229 --> 00:28:11,524
Eating people alive?
Where does that get fun?

498
00:28:13,109 --> 00:28:15,445
Shepherd Book said
they was men who just

499
00:28:15,528 --> 00:28:18,865
reached the edge of space,
saw a vasty nothingness

500
00:28:18,948 --> 00:28:20,950
and went bibbledy
over it.

501
00:28:21,075 --> 00:28:22,076
Oh, hell.

502
00:28:22,327 --> 00:28:23,661
(CLANKING)

503
00:28:23,870 --> 00:28:25,455
JAYNE: I've been
to the edge.

504
00:28:26,122 --> 00:28:30,001
