752
00:43:34,154 --> 00:43:35,697
Put a bullet to me.

753
00:43:36,698 --> 00:43:39,284
Bullet in the
brainpan, squish.

754
00:43:39,368 --> 00:43:40,702
(SOBBING)

755
00:43:41,370 --> 00:43:44,039
Don't say that.
Not ever.

756
00:43:46,667 --> 00:43:48,335
We'll get through this.

757
00:43:51,171 --> 00:43:53,882
Things are going to
get much, much worse.

758
00:44:00,139 --> 00:44:01,640
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

759
00:44:01,723 --> 00:44:03,225
(WATER RUNNING)

760
00:44:28,625 --> 00:44:30,127
(CHATTERING)

761
00:44:47,895 --> 00:44:50,189
MAL: Thanks for taking
us in again, Shepherd.

762
00:44:50,898 --> 00:44:52,191
SHEPHERD: You got a plan?

763
00:44:52,941 --> 00:44:54,276
Hiding ain't a plan?

764
00:44:54,359 --> 00:44:56,028
It'll do you
for a spell.

765
00:44:56,111 --> 00:44:58,197
And the folks here'll be
glad of the extra coin.

766
00:44:58,280 --> 00:45:00,324
But the Alliance
will be coming.

767
00:45:00,574 --> 00:45:03,118
They're after this girl
with a powerful will.

768
00:45:03,911 --> 00:45:06,788
I look to hear the tromp
of their boots any moment.

769
00:45:09,166 --> 00:45:10,500
You won't.

770
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:15,631
This isn't a palms-up
military run, Mal.

771
00:45:17,090 --> 00:45:18,800
No reports broadwaved,

772
00:45:19,551 --> 00:45:20,719
no warrants.

773
00:45:21,178 --> 00:45:23,597
Much as they want her,
they want her hid.

774
00:45:24,181 --> 00:45:26,099
That means
closed file.

775
00:45:26,975 --> 00:45:28,477
Means an operative.

776
00:45:29,478 --> 00:45:31,563
Which is trouble
you've not known.

777
00:45:33,982 --> 00:45:35,859
I could have
left her there.

778
00:45:38,237 --> 00:45:39,488
I had an out.

779
00:45:40,280 --> 00:45:42,407
<i>Hell, I had every
reason in the 'verse</i>

780
00:45:42,491 --> 00:45:44,660
<i>to leave her lay
and haul anchor.</i>

781
00:45:45,661 --> 00:45:47,329
It's not your
way, Mal.

782
00:45:48,830 --> 00:45:50,123
I have a way?

783
00:45:51,166 --> 00:45:52,834
That better
than a plan?

784
00:45:53,377 --> 00:45:56,672
Only one thing is gonna
walk you through this, Mal.

785
00:45:58,632 --> 00:45:59,633
Belief.

786
00:46:01,551 --> 00:46:03,720
You know I always look
to you for counsel,

787
00:46:03,804 --> 00:46:06,014
but sermons make me
sleepy, Shepherd.

788
00:46:06,723 --> 00:46:09,059
I ain't looking for
help from on high.

789
00:46:10,310 --> 00:46:12,479
That's a long wait
for a train don't come.

790
00:46:12,562 --> 00:46:16,525
When I talk about belief, why do you
always assume I'm talking about God?

791
00:46:22,531 --> 00:46:24,700
They'll come at
you sideways.

792
00:46:25,492 --> 00:46:27,953
It's how they think.
It's how they move.

793
00:46:29,162 --> 00:46:32,958
Sidle up and smile. Hit
you where you're weak.

794
00:46:34,584 --> 00:46:37,546
Sort of man they're like
to send believes hard.

795
00:46:38,714 --> 00:46:40,757
Kills and never
asks why.

796
00:46:45,846 --> 00:46:48,640
It's of interest to me how much you
seem to know about that world.

797
00:46:48,724 --> 00:46:50,892
I wasn't born
a Shepherd, Mal.

798
00:46:50,976 --> 00:46:53,228
Have to tell me
about that sometime.

799
00:46:53,437 --> 00:46:54,646
(SIGHING)

800
00:46:55,105 --> 00:46:56,648
No, I don't.

801
00:47:00,444 --> 00:47:01,611
WOMAN: River?

802
00:47:02,821 --> 00:47:04,489
River, you look tired.

803
00:47:04,781 --> 00:47:08,577
I think everybody's a little tired by now.
Why don't we all lie down?

804
00:47:09,578 --> 00:47:12,581
A little peace and quiet
will make everything better.

805
00:47:12,748 --> 00:47:14,166
River. Do as
you're told.

806
00:47:14,249 --> 00:47:15,292
No.

807
00:47:15,375 --> 00:47:17,336
It's going to be
fine. Lie down.

808
00:47:17,419 --> 00:47:18,420
No.

809
00:47:22,341 --> 00:47:23,592
<i>MAN: Cut them down.</i>

810
00:47:27,346 --> 00:47:28,347
(MUMBLING) What?

811
00:47:28,430 --> 00:47:30,265
<i>WASH: Mal! You up?</i>

812
00:47:31,099 --> 00:47:33,769
<i>I got a wave. I'm gonna
bounce it down to you.</i>

813
00:47:39,191 --> 00:47:40,192
Inara.

814
00:47:41,109 --> 00:47:43,945
<i>I... Is this
a bad time?</i>

815
00:47:44,863 --> 00:47:47,783
No, it's good as any.

816
00:47:48,283 --> 00:47:49,326
How's your world?

817
00:47:49,409 --> 00:47:50,994
<i>Cold. It's autumn here.</i>

818
00:47:51,495 --> 00:47:53,330
Still at the
Training House?

819
00:47:55,082 --> 00:47:56,666
<i>(CLEARING THROAT)</i>

820
00:47:57,292 --> 00:48:01,463
So, what occasions the wave?
Not that to see you ain't...

821
00:48:03,298 --> 00:48:05,008
Well, you look very fine.

822
00:48:05,092 --> 00:48:06,426
<i>Oh. Thank you.</i>

823
00:48:06,802 --> 00:48:08,595
<i>MAL: So, what was the...</i>

824
00:48:11,014 --> 00:48:14,267
<i>I guess we're having something of
a problem here with the locals.</i>

825
00:48:14,351 --> 00:48:15,394
<i>And, I thought
maybe...</i>

826
00:48:15,477 --> 00:48:16,978
You could use a gun hand?

827
00:48:17,062 --> 00:48:21,233
<i>I'm hoping not. But if you happen
to be close at all, you...</i>

828
00:48:21,358 --> 00:48:25,362
<i>The crew could take your ease
here for a while. And there'd be payment.</i>

829
00:48:27,989 --> 00:48:31,243
Well, it would be...
I mean, I'd like to.

830
00:48:35,497 --> 00:48:38,083
Kaylee's been missing
you something fierce.

831
00:48:38,166 --> 00:48:39,835
<i>ALL: Oh, man.
I miss her, too.</i>

832
00:48:39,918 --> 00:48:42,003
<i>I even miss my shuttle,
occasionally.</i>

833
00:48:42,087 --> 00:48:44,172
Yeah, you left...

834
00:48:44,548 --> 00:48:46,258
Got some of your
stuff in a trunk.

835
00:48:46,341 --> 00:48:47,884
I never did get a
chance to drop it off.

836
00:48:47,968 --> 00:48:50,011
<i>(STAMMERING) I didn't
mean to leave stuff.</i>

837
00:48:50,095 --> 00:48:52,222
I didn't look
through the stuff.

838
00:48:52,556 --> 00:48:55,725
I just... Just
sundries, I expect.

839
00:48:58,645 --> 00:49:01,440
So I'll send you a
wave, soon as I can.

840
00:49:02,190 --> 00:49:03,358
<i>Thank you.</i>

841
00:49:12,325 --> 00:49:15,203
Inara, nice to
see her again.

842
00:49:17,164 --> 00:49:18,874
So, trap?

843
00:49:18,957 --> 00:49:19,958
Trap.

844
00:49:20,041 --> 00:49:21,209
ZOE: We going in?

845
00:49:21,293 --> 00:49:22,711
Only but a
few hours out.

846
00:49:23,336 --> 00:49:26,339
Yeah, but, remember the
part where it's a trap?

847
00:49:26,548 --> 00:49:28,967
If that's the case, then
Inara's already caught in it.

848
00:49:29,050 --> 00:49:31,052
She wouldn't set
us up willing.

849
00:49:31,261 --> 00:49:34,139
Might be we got a shot at seeing
who's turning these wheels.

850
00:49:34,222 --> 00:49:35,223
We go in.

851
00:49:35,307 --> 00:49:38,643
But how can you be sure Inara
don't just wanna see you?

852
00:49:39,561 --> 00:49:41,980
Sometimes people
have feelings.

853
00:49:42,147 --> 00:49:44,191
I'm referring
here to people.

854
00:49:45,942 --> 00:49:48,069
You all were watching,
I take it.

855
00:49:49,738 --> 00:49:50,739
Yes.

856
00:49:50,822 --> 00:49:51,823
Did you see
us fight?

857
00:49:51,907 --> 00:49:52,908
No.

858
00:49:52,991 --> 00:49:54,075
Trap.

859
00:50:01,500 --> 00:50:05,337
We're about 70 miles from the
Training House, and nobody on radar.

860
00:50:05,420 --> 00:50:07,839
If the Alliance is about,
they're laying low.

861
00:50:07,923 --> 00:50:09,090
They're about.

862
00:50:09,174 --> 00:50:11,176
Find us a home. I'll take the
shuttle a little closer.

863
00:50:11,259 --> 00:50:12,928
Zoe, ship
is yours.

864
00:50:13,011 --> 00:50:15,514
Remember. If anything
happens to me,

865
00:50:15,597 --> 00:50:17,307
or if you don't hear
from me within the hour,

866
00:50:17,390 --> 00:50:19,684
you take this ship and you
come and you rescue me.

867
00:50:19,768 --> 00:50:20,769
What?

868
00:50:21,394 --> 00:50:22,771
Risk my ship?

869
00:50:22,854 --> 00:50:24,022
I mean it.

870
00:50:24,105 --> 00:50:26,858
It's cold out there. And
I don't wanna get left.

871
00:50:43,708 --> 00:50:47,045
Dear Buddha, please bring me a
pony, and a plastic rocket, and...

872
00:50:47,128 --> 00:50:49,047
Mal! What are
you doing here?

873
00:50:49,631 --> 00:50:50,840
Well, you invited me.

874
00:50:50,924 --> 00:50:53,468
I never thought for a second
you'd be stupid enough to come.

875
00:50:53,552 --> 00:50:55,387
Well, that makes you kind
of a tease, doesn't it?

876
00:50:55,470 --> 00:50:57,389
You knew my invitation
wasn't on the level.

877
00:50:57,472 --> 00:51:00,433
Which led me to conclude that
you must be in some trouble.

878
00:51:00,517 --> 00:51:02,269
I'm fine. I'm giddy.

879
00:51:02,352 --> 00:51:04,771
For a woman schooled in telling
a man what he wants to hear,

880
00:51:04,854 --> 00:51:06,231
you ain't much of a liar.

881
00:51:06,314 --> 00:51:08,358
Mal, you cannot
handle this man.

882
00:51:14,447 --> 00:51:15,574
I have to say, Captain,

883
00:51:15,657 --> 00:51:18,535
I'm impressed that you would
come for her yourself.

884
00:51:18,827 --> 00:51:21,955
And that you would make it
this far, in that outfit.

885
00:51:23,164 --> 00:51:25,417
I can be very graceful
when I need to.

886
00:51:25,500 --> 00:51:26,876
I've no doubt.

887
00:51:28,295 --> 00:51:29,296
What are you doing?

888
00:51:29,379 --> 00:51:31,006
I'm praying for you, Mal.

889
00:51:31,715 --> 00:51:33,508
She's very thoughtful.

890
00:51:33,925 --> 00:51:36,886
But I mean it when I say
I've no intent to harm you.

891
00:51:37,679 --> 00:51:39,306
Speak your piece.

892
00:51:39,764 --> 00:51:41,600
I think you're beginning
to understand

893
00:51:41,683 --> 00:51:43,643
how dangerous River Tam is.

894
00:51:44,019 --> 00:51:45,854
She is a mite
unpredictable.

895
00:51:46,104 --> 00:51:47,981
Mood swings,
of a sort.

896
00:51:48,064 --> 00:51:49,357
It's worse
than you know.

897
00:51:49,441 --> 00:51:50,609
It usually is.

898
00:51:50,692 --> 00:51:54,321
That girl will rain destruction
down on you and your ship.

899
00:51:55,697 --> 00:51:58,491
She is an albatross,
Captain.

900
00:51:58,617 --> 00:52:00,368
Way I remember it,

901
00:52:00,493 --> 00:52:03,830
albatross was a ship's good luck,
till some idiot killed it.

902
00:52:04,372 --> 00:52:07,042
Yes, I've read a poem.
Try not to faint.

903
00:52:07,584 --> 00:52:09,419
I've seen your
war record.

904
00:52:10,378 --> 00:52:12,964
I know how you must
feel about the Alliance.

905
00:52:13,214 --> 00:52:14,299
You really don't.

906
00:52:14,382 --> 00:52:15,425
Fair to say.

907
00:52:16,176 --> 00:52:18,970
But I have to hope you
understand, you can't beat us.

908
00:52:19,054 --> 00:52:20,805
I got no need
to beat you.

909
00:52:20,889 --> 00:52:22,140
I just want
to go my way.

910
00:52:22,223 --> 00:52:23,725
And you can do that,

911
00:52:24,559 --> 00:52:27,604
once you let me take
River Tam back home.

912
00:52:31,316 --> 00:52:33,860
No, no. You're working
this deal all crabbed.

913
00:52:33,943 --> 00:52:35,278
You got to open
with payment.

914
00:52:35,362 --> 00:52:36,655
That is a trap.

915
00:52:36,738 --> 00:52:40,325
I offer money, you'll play the
man of honor and take umbrage.

916
00:52:40,575 --> 00:52:43,161
I ask you to do what is right,
you'll play the brigand.

917
00:52:43,244 --> 00:52:45,747
I have no stomach
for games.

918
00:52:46,289 --> 00:52:48,291
I already know you
will not see reason.

919
00:52:48,375 --> 00:52:49,918
The Alliance wanted
to show me a reason,

920
00:52:50,001 --> 00:52:52,212
they shouldn't have
sent an assassin.

921
00:52:58,426 --> 00:53:01,554
I have a warship in
deep orbit, Captain.

922
00:53:02,180 --> 00:53:05,767
We locked on to <i>Serenity's</i> pulse
beacon the moment you hit atmo.

923
00:53:05,892 --> 00:53:07,852
I can speak a word
and send a missile

924
00:53:07,936 --> 00:53:10,689
to that exact location
inside of three minutes.

925
00:53:10,772 --> 00:53:11,940
You do that,

926
00:53:13,024 --> 00:53:15,902
you'd best make peace with
your dear and fluffy lord.

927
00:53:19,656 --> 00:53:20,907
Pulse beacon.

928
00:53:21,157 --> 00:53:25,120
Advice from an old tracker. You want
to find someone, use your eyes.

929
00:53:25,620 --> 00:53:27,872
How long do you think you
can really run from us?

930
00:53:27,956 --> 00:53:30,542
I never credited the Alliance
with an overabundance of brains.

931
00:53:30,625 --> 00:53:31,668
And if you're
the best they got...

932
00:53:31,751 --> 00:53:32,877
Captain Reynolds,

933
00:53:32,961 --> 00:53:35,714
I should tell you, so that
you don't waste your time,

934
00:53:35,797 --> 00:53:38,174
you can't make me angry.

935
00:53:38,258 --> 00:53:39,801
Please, spend
an hour with him.

936
00:53:40,510 --> 00:53:43,304
I want to resolve this
like civilized men.

937
00:53:44,389 --> 00:53:46,307
I'm not
threatening you.

938
00:53:46,641 --> 00:53:48,143
I'm unarmed.
Good.

939
00:53:53,231 --> 00:53:55,275
I am, of course, wearing
full body armor.

940
00:53:55,358 --> 00:53:56,401
I am not a moron.

941
00:53:56,484 --> 00:53:57,694
INARA: Wait, just let...

942
00:53:57,819 --> 00:53:59,821
(GRUNTING)

943
00:54:14,502 --> 00:54:15,795
(GLASS SHATTERING)

944
00:54:15,879 --> 00:54:17,046
(GROANS)

945
00:54:21,259 --> 00:54:23,386
(PANTING)

946
00:54:23,470 --> 00:54:24,804
(GASPING)

947
00:54:25,889 --> 00:54:27,390
What, no backup?

948
00:54:27,891 --> 00:54:29,184
Making an awful ruckus.

949
00:54:29,267 --> 00:54:31,102
They'll come when
they're needed.

950
00:54:31,186 --> 00:54:32,604
I'd start whistling.

951
00:54:32,729 --> 00:54:35,899
Captain, what do you think
is going to happen here?

952
00:54:38,777 --> 00:54:40,904
(BOTH GRUNTING)

953
00:54:47,702 --> 00:54:48,745
(GROANS)

954
00:54:52,749 --> 00:54:53,958
(RIPPING)

955
00:54:58,963 --> 00:55:00,256
(CLATTERING)

956
00:55:00,548 --> 00:55:01,633
(GROANING)

957
00:55:11,851 --> 00:55:13,228
(GLASS SHATTERS)

958
00:55:14,562 --> 00:55:15,688
(PANTING)

959
00:55:22,737 --> 00:55:27,075
Nothing here is what it seems.
He isn't the plucky hero.

960
00:55:27,909 --> 00:55:31,871
The Alliance isn't some evil empire.
This is not the grand arena.

961
00:55:32,080 --> 00:55:33,748
And that's not incense.

962
00:55:36,960 --> 00:55:38,586
(BEEPING)

963
00:55:40,755 --> 00:55:41,923
Sir, can you hear me?

964
00:55:42,006 --> 00:55:44,551
Just a flash bomb.
Go. Go!

965
00:55:45,134 --> 00:55:47,262
(INARA AND MAL GRUNTING)

966
00:55:50,265 --> 00:55:51,766
What have you done
to my shuttle?

967
00:55:51,850 --> 00:55:53,476
It's not your shuttle.

968
00:55:53,852 --> 00:55:55,728
Head east. Keep her low.

969
00:55:55,979 --> 00:55:57,772
(ENGINE REVVING)

970
00:56:11,536 --> 00:56:13,371
Okay, forget the
pulse beacon.

971
00:56:13,454 --> 00:56:15,582
<i>There must be another
way to track the ship.</i>

972
00:56:15,665 --> 00:56:17,041
Get a read on
the nav. sat.

973
00:56:17,125 --> 00:56:19,711
It's a registered transport,
you must be able to locate.

974
00:56:19,794 --> 00:56:20,753
<i>ENSIGN: Sir?</i>

975
00:56:20,837 --> 00:56:22,714
Yes, have you found
a nav. sat. trajectory?

976
00:56:22,797 --> 00:56:25,216
<i>Sir, we found seven.</i>

977
00:56:32,932 --> 00:56:34,642
<i>INARA: We've every
reason to be afraid.</i>

978
00:56:35,101 --> 00:56:38,062
Why, 'cause this guy beat up Mal?
That ain't so hard.

979
00:56:38,146 --> 00:56:40,690
He didn't beat me up.
Nobody said that.

980
00:56:40,773 --> 00:56:42,525
Because he's a believer.

981
00:56:42,775 --> 00:56:47,196
He's intelligent, methodical,
and devout in his belief

982
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:49,657
that killing River is
the right thing to do.

983
00:56:49,741 --> 00:56:52,327
So no hope of
a reward, huh?

984
00:56:53,244 --> 00:56:56,664
Did he say anything
about a Miranda?

985
00:56:57,498 --> 00:56:58,541
What is that?

986
00:56:58,625 --> 00:57:01,002
Don't know who or what,
but it's on River's mind.

987
00:57:01,085 --> 00:57:03,087
Conjure it might be the
reason they're after her.

988
00:57:03,171 --> 00:57:06,049
You think maybe it poses some
kind of threat to the Alliance?

989
00:57:06,132 --> 00:57:07,508
Do we care?

990
00:57:07,884 --> 00:57:09,594
Are we caring
about that?

991
00:57:09,677 --> 00:57:12,305
You dumb-ass hogs, the only
people she's a threat to is

992
00:57:12,388 --> 00:57:13,890
us on this boat.

993
00:57:13,973 --> 00:57:16,017
Look, we get back to Haven
in a few hours' time.

994
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:18,269
Oh, yeah. Hiding under
the Shepherd's skirts

995
00:57:18,353 --> 00:57:19,354
that's a manful scheme.

996
00:57:19,437 --> 00:57:20,480
You wanna run
this ship?

997
00:57:20,563 --> 00:57:21,689
Yes.

998
00:57:22,523 --> 00:57:24,359
Well, you can't.

999
00:57:25,068 --> 00:57:27,278
Do a damn sight
better job than you.

1000
00:57:27,362 --> 00:57:29,822
Getting us lashed over
a couple of strays.

1001
00:57:30,031 --> 00:57:32,033
No offense, Doc. I think
it's noble as a grape,

1002
00:57:32,116 --> 00:57:33,326
the way you
look to River.

1003
00:57:33,409 --> 00:57:35,870
But she ain't my sister
and she ain't your crew.

1004
00:57:35,954 --> 00:57:38,331
Oh, and neither is
she exactly helpless.

1005
00:57:38,706 --> 00:57:41,209
So where's it writ that we got
to lay down our lives for her?

1006
00:57:41,292 --> 00:57:42,835
Which is what you've
steered us toward.

1007
00:57:42,919 --> 00:57:44,671
I didn't start this.

1008
00:57:45,254 --> 00:57:46,839
No, that's right.

1009
00:57:47,674 --> 00:57:51,344
Alliance starts the war,
and then you volunteer.

1010
00:57:53,262 --> 00:57:54,973
Battle of Serenity, Mal.

1011
00:57:55,056 --> 00:57:58,267
Besides Zoe here, how many...
Hey, I'm talking at you.

1012
00:58:02,313 --> 00:58:05,358
How many men in your platoon
came out of there alive?

1013
00:58:08,569 --> 00:58:10,738
You wanna leave this room.

1014
00:58:13,574 --> 00:58:15,284
Damn right, I do.

1015
00:58:22,625 --> 00:58:24,669
This isn't
the war, Mal.

1016
00:58:25,545 --> 00:58:27,755
You telling me that 'cause
you think I don't know?

1017
00:58:27,839 --> 00:58:29,966
You came to the Training
House looking for a fight.

1018
00:58:30,049 --> 00:58:31,926
I came looking
for you.

1019
00:58:33,261 --> 00:58:35,680
I just want to know
who I'm dealing with.

1020
00:58:35,763 --> 00:58:38,433
I've seen too many versions
of you to be sure.

1021
00:58:38,683 --> 00:58:42,937
I start fighting a war, I guarantee
you'll see something new.

1022
00:58:50,111 --> 00:58:51,320
We'll get off.

1023
00:58:51,404 --> 00:58:53,031
River and I will
get off at Haven.

1024
00:58:53,114 --> 00:58:54,866
We'll find some...
Nobody's saying that.

1025
00:58:54,949 --> 00:58:56,743
Nobody besides Jayne
is saying that.

1026
00:58:56,826 --> 00:58:57,827
Mal.

1027
00:59:00,329 --> 00:59:03,416
I got no answers for you, Inara.
I got no rudder.

1028
00:59:03,499 --> 00:59:06,461
Wind blows northerly, I go north.
That's who I am.

1029
00:59:06,544 --> 00:59:09,088
Now maybe that ain't a man to
lead, but they have to follow.

1030
00:59:09,172 --> 00:59:10,256
So you wanna
tear me down,

1031
00:59:10,339 --> 00:59:11,382
do it inside
your own mind.

1032
00:59:11,466 --> 00:59:12,508
I'm not trying
to tear you down.

1033
00:59:12,592 --> 00:59:14,177
But you fog things up.

1034
00:59:14,969 --> 00:59:16,679
You always have.

1035
00:59:18,306 --> 00:59:19,766
You spin me about.

1036
00:59:22,977 --> 00:59:25,104
I wish like hell
you was elsewhere.

1037
00:59:25,188 --> 00:59:26,272
(SIGHS)

1038
00:59:27,315 --> 00:59:28,441
I was.

1039
01:00:08,022 --> 01:00:09,524
(RUMBLING)

1040
01:00:19,367 --> 01:00:20,868
(FLIES BUZZING)

1041
01:00:23,788 --> 01:00:24,914
(GASPS)

1042
01:00:49,021 --> 01:00:50,523
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

1043
01:00:59,323 --> 01:01:00,575
(BEEPING)

1044
01:01:01,576 --> 01:01:03,828
No trouble,
little crazy person.

1045
01:01:05,830 --> 01:01:09,208
We're going for
a nice shuttle ride.

1046
01:01:12,795 --> 01:01:13,921
(GUN FIRES)

1047
01:01:21,596 --> 01:01:23,306
(DOORKNOB RATTLING)

1048
01:01:26,726 --> 01:01:28,519
She's out. Jayne's down.

1049
01:01:28,728 --> 01:01:31,272
The other way. Find her
and do not engage.

1050
01:01:44,869 --> 01:01:46,162
(BEEPING)

1051
01:01:53,628 --> 01:01:55,129
It's gonna be okay...

1052
01:01:55,880 --> 01:01:57,131
(COUGHS)

1053
01:02:05,723 --> 01:02:07,892
She's sealed off the bridge.
I do not like her there.

1054
01:02:07,975 --> 01:02:09,644
Check the shuttle. She
could have snuck in.

1055
01:02:09,727 --> 01:02:10,728
Captain.

1056
01:02:44,220 --> 01:02:45,846
(COMPUTER BEEPS)

1057
01:02:56,774 --> 01:02:59,694
The government's man, he
says you're a danger to us.

1058
01:03:00,695 --> 01:03:02,321
Not worth helping.

1059
01:03:04,907 --> 01:03:06,075
Is he right?

1060
01:03:07,368 --> 01:03:09,787
Are you anything
but a weapon?

1061
01:03:12,999 --> 01:03:16,085
I've staked my crew's life on
the theory you're a person,

1062
01:03:16,168 --> 01:03:19,297
actual and whole, and if I'm
wrong, you'd best shoot me now.

1063
01:03:19,380 --> 01:03:20,423
(CLICKS)

1064
01:03:20,506 --> 01:03:22,383
Or we could talk more.

1065
01:03:33,519 --> 01:03:34,603
Miranda.

1066
01:03:38,733 --> 01:03:41,110
How can it be there's a
whole planet called Miranda

1067
01:03:41,193 --> 01:03:42,445
and none of us
knowed that?

1068
01:03:42,528 --> 01:03:45,906
Because there isn't one.
It's a blackrock. Uninhabitable.

1069
01:03:46,407 --> 01:03:49,452
Terraforming didn't hold, or some such.
Few settlers died.

1070
01:03:49,535 --> 01:03:50,995
ZOE: Was it right
before the war?

1071
01:03:51,078 --> 01:03:54,957
I had to show them. I didn't know
if you were going to make me sleep.

1072
01:03:56,584 --> 01:03:57,626
You could
have asked.

1073
01:03:57,710 --> 01:03:58,794
KAYLEE: Wait
a tick, yeah.

1074
01:03:58,878 --> 01:04:02,465
Some years back, there was call
for workers to settle on Miranda.

1075
01:04:02,590 --> 01:04:04,342
Daddy talked about it. Nothing
about it on the Cortex.

1076
01:04:04,425 --> 01:04:06,427
History, Astronomy,
it's not in there.

1077
01:04:06,510 --> 01:04:08,846
Half of writing history
is hiding the truth.

1078
01:04:08,929 --> 01:04:11,849
There's something on that rock
the Alliance doesn't want known.

1079
01:04:11,932 --> 01:04:14,101
That's right at the edge of
the Burnham Quadrant, right?

1080
01:04:14,185 --> 01:04:16,520
Furthest planet out? It's
not that far from here.

1081
01:04:16,604 --> 01:04:18,314
Whoa. No. No. Honey...
That's a bad notion.

1082
01:04:18,439 --> 01:04:20,775
...you show them the bad.
I got it, baby.

1083
01:04:24,445 --> 01:04:27,114
This is us, at Haven,
and here's Miranda.

1084
01:04:27,656 --> 01:04:31,869
All along here, that empty space in
between, that's Reaver territory.

1085
01:04:31,952 --> 01:04:34,580
They just float out there,
sending out raiding parties.

1086
01:04:34,663 --> 01:04:36,999
ZOE: Nobody ventures there.
Not even the Alliance.

1087
01:04:37,083 --> 01:04:39,335
You go through that, you're
signing up to be a banquet.

1088
01:04:39,418 --> 01:04:42,004
I'm on board with our standard
run-and-hide scenario.

1089
01:04:42,088 --> 01:04:43,798
And we are just about...

1090
01:04:44,632 --> 01:04:45,633
Wait.

1091
01:05:02,983 --> 01:05:04,235
JAYNE: Doesn't
look like Reavers.

1092
01:05:04,318 --> 01:05:05,444
Wasn't.

1093
01:05:10,991 --> 01:05:11,992
KAYLEE: Shepherd?

1094
01:05:13,786 --> 01:05:14,912
Shepherd?

1095
01:05:16,247 --> 01:05:17,498
KAYLEE: Shepherd Book?

1096
01:05:35,724 --> 01:05:36,767
(COCKING GUN)

1097
01:05:36,851 --> 01:05:38,185
(MAN COUGHING)

1098
01:05:38,561 --> 01:05:40,020
Get the Doc.

1099
01:05:41,230 --> 01:05:42,273
Shepherd.

1100
01:05:42,356 --> 01:05:43,441
(GASPING)

1101
01:05:43,524 --> 01:05:44,608
Don't move.

1102
01:05:44,692 --> 01:05:46,360
Won't go far.

1103
01:05:48,988 --> 01:05:50,990
Shouldn't have
been you.

1104
01:05:51,782 --> 01:05:54,410
Alliance should've hit
us. Should've hit me.

1105
01:05:55,786 --> 01:05:57,538
That crossed my mind.

1106
01:05:58,122 --> 01:05:59,582
(COUGHING)

1107
01:06:02,042 --> 01:06:03,461
I shot him down.

1108
01:06:03,544 --> 01:06:05,212
Yeah. I see.

1109
01:06:05,421 --> 01:06:08,007
I killed the ship
that killed us.

1110
01:06:09,717 --> 01:06:11,719
Not very Christian of me.

1111
01:06:12,178 --> 01:06:13,721
You did what's right.

1112
01:06:14,180 --> 01:06:18,225
Coming from you, that
means almost nothing.

1113
01:06:20,978 --> 01:06:22,188
(COUGHING)

1114
01:06:23,564 --> 01:06:24,648
I'm long gone.

1115
01:06:24,732 --> 01:06:26,358
No, Doc will
bring you around.

1116
01:06:26,442 --> 01:06:29,320
I look to be bored by many
more sermons before you slip.

1117
01:06:29,403 --> 01:06:30,696
Just don't move.

1118
01:06:31,280 --> 01:06:33,073
Can't order me
around, boy.

1119
01:06:34,408 --> 01:06:36,160
I'm not one
of your crew.

1120
01:06:38,245 --> 01:06:39,663
Yes, you are.

1121
01:06:42,500 --> 01:06:44,376
River...
Come on.

1122
01:06:44,793 --> 01:06:45,794
Hey.

1123
01:06:47,588 --> 01:06:51,550
I don't care what you believe.
Just believe it.

1124
01:06:53,219 --> 01:06:55,012
Whatever you...

1125
01:07:28,462 --> 01:07:30,506
How come they
ain't waiting?

1126
01:07:31,674 --> 01:07:34,635
They knowed we was coming,
how come they only sent one?

1127
01:07:35,803 --> 01:07:38,138
They didn't know
we were coming here.

1128
01:07:38,889 --> 01:07:40,599
Get on the Cortex.

1129
01:07:40,683 --> 01:07:42,560
Wave, Li Shen,
the Sanchez brothers,

1130
01:07:42,643 --> 01:07:44,603
anyone who has ever
sheltered us after a heist.

1131
01:07:44,687 --> 01:07:46,146
Tell them to get out.

1132
01:07:46,230 --> 01:07:47,481
Get out now.

1133
01:07:58,659 --> 01:07:59,827
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

1134
01:08:01,954 --> 01:08:05,708
<i>If your quarry goes to ground,
leave no ground to go to.</i>

1135
01:08:06,834 --> 01:08:08,877
<i>You should have
taken my offer.</i>

1136
01:08:08,961 --> 01:08:11,505
<i>Or did you think none
of this was your fault?</i>

1137
01:08:11,797 --> 01:08:13,757
I don't murder children.

1138
01:08:14,174 --> 01:08:15,175
<i>I do.</i>

1139
01:08:16,093 --> 01:08:18,137
<i>If I have to.
Why'?</i>

1140
01:08:20,014 --> 01:08:22,182
Do you even know
why they sent you?

1141
01:08:22,933 --> 01:08:24,685
<i>It's not my
place to ask.</i>

1142
01:08:25,894 --> 01:08:28,439
<i>I believe in something
greater than myself.</i>

1143
01:08:29,565 --> 01:08:30,983
<i>A better world.</i>

1144
01:08:31,609 --> 01:08:33,444
<i>A world without sin.</i>

1145
01:08:33,986 --> 01:08:35,946
So me and mine gotta
lay down and die

1146
01:08:36,030 --> 01:08:38,240
so you can live in
your better world?

1147
01:08:38,699 --> 01:08:40,868
<i>I'm not going to live there.</i>

1148
01:08:41,243 --> 01:08:42,828
<i>There's no place
for me there</i>

1149
01:08:42,911 --> 01:08:45,372
<i>any more than there
is for you. Malcolm,</i>

1150
01:08:45,539 --> 01:08:46,790
<i>I'm a monster.</i>

1151
01:08:48,459 --> 01:08:49,752
<i>What I do is evil.</i>

1152
01:08:49,835 --> 01:08:52,379
<i>I have no illusions about
it, but it must be done.</i>

1153
01:08:52,504 --> 01:08:53,964
Keep talking.

1154
01:08:54,256 --> 01:08:56,300
You're not getting a location
trace off this wave.

1155
01:08:56,383 --> 01:09:00,304
<i>And every minute you keep River Tam
from me, more people will die.</i>

1156
01:09:00,387 --> 01:09:01,430
You think I care?

1157
01:09:01,513 --> 01:09:02,890
<i>Of course you care.</i>

1158
01:09:03,807 --> 01:09:05,559
<i>You're not a Reaver, Mal.</i>

1159
01:09:06,060 --> 01:09:09,563
<i>You're a human man and you
will never understand how...</i>

1160
01:09:15,819 --> 01:09:17,613
Get these bodies together.

1161
01:09:18,113 --> 01:09:19,406
ZOE: We got time
for grave digging?

1162
01:09:19,490 --> 01:09:20,824
Zoe, you and Simon
rope them together.

1163
01:09:20,908 --> 01:09:23,619
Five or six of them. I want them
laid out on the nose of our ship.

1164
01:09:23,702 --> 01:09:25,996
Are you insane? I won't
desecrate these bodies.

1165
01:09:26,080 --> 01:09:27,915
I don't understand. What
do you mean, the bodies...

1166
01:09:27,998 --> 01:09:29,458
I want you to muck up
the reactor core.

1167
01:09:29,541 --> 01:09:31,543
Just enough to leave a trail
and make it read like

1168
01:09:31,627 --> 01:09:33,754
we're flying without containment,
not enough to fry us.

1169
01:09:33,879 --> 01:09:35,673
These people are our friends.
Kaylee,

1170
01:09:35,756 --> 01:09:38,592
you got a day's work to do
and two hours to do it.

1171
01:09:39,593 --> 01:09:43,847
Jayne, you and Wash hoist up
the cannon mount. Goes right on top.

1172
01:09:43,931 --> 01:09:45,599
Piece or two of the other
ship, stick it on.

1173
01:09:45,683 --> 01:09:48,936
Any place you can tear hull without
inner breach, do that, too.

1174
01:09:49,770 --> 01:09:53,107
We're gonna need paint.
We're gonna need red paint.

1175
01:09:53,524 --> 01:09:54,525
Sir,

1176
01:09:54,983 --> 01:09:58,404
do you really mean to turn
our home into an abomination

1177
01:09:58,487 --> 01:10:00,322
so that we can make
a suicidal attempt

1178
01:10:00,406 --> 01:10:02,449
at passing through
Reaver space?

1179
01:10:02,533 --> 01:10:03,826
I mean to live.

1180
01:10:04,284 --> 01:10:05,703
(MAN COUGHING)
I mean for us to live.

1181
01:10:05,786 --> 01:10:08,330
The Alliance won't have that, so
we go where they don't follow.

1182
01:10:08,414 --> 01:10:10,582
God's balls, there ain't no
way we're going out there.

1183
01:10:10,666 --> 01:10:12,000
Think about what
you're asking.

1184
01:10:12,084 --> 01:10:14,253
JAYNE: Those Reavers'll
eat us alive...

1185
01:10:16,380 --> 01:10:17,798
This is how it is.

1186
01:10:18,215 --> 01:10:19,883
Anybody doesn't wanna
fly with me anymore,

1187
01:10:19,967 --> 01:10:21,802
this is your port
of harbor.

1188
01:10:22,678 --> 01:10:24,722
There's a lot of
fine ways to die.

1189
01:10:24,805 --> 01:10:27,516
I ain't waiting for the
Alliance to choose mine.

1190
01:10:31,103 --> 01:10:34,273
I mean to confound these bungers.
Take my shot at getting to Miranda.

1191
01:10:34,356 --> 01:10:36,900
Maybe find something I can
use to get clear of this.

1192
01:10:36,984 --> 01:10:39,903
So I hear a word out of any of
you that ain't helping me out

1193
01:10:39,987 --> 01:10:42,489
or taking your leave,
I will shoot you down.

1194
01:10:47,453 --> 01:10:48,787
Get to work.

1195
01:11:13,937 --> 01:11:14,938
ZOE: Sir...

1196
01:11:15,022 --> 01:11:16,565
Just tell me
when we're close.

1197
01:11:52,726 --> 01:11:54,770
<i>(PEOPLE SCREAMING)</i>

1198
01:12:24,466 --> 01:12:25,467
MAL: Wash.

1199
01:13:30,115 --> 01:13:33,327
Define "disappeared."

1200
01:13:38,081 --> 01:13:40,334
ZOE: Every reading
I'm getting says normal.

1201
01:13:41,043 --> 01:13:44,379
Oceans, land masses. No tectonic
instability or radiation.

1202
01:13:44,463 --> 01:13:46,048
Yeah, but no
power, either.

1203
01:13:46,131 --> 01:13:47,424
Nothing at all?

1204
01:13:47,507 --> 01:13:48,508
Wait.

1205
01:13:49,176 --> 01:13:50,302
Something.

1206
01:13:51,345 --> 01:13:53,847
It might be a beacon,
but it's awful weak.

1207
01:13:54,514 --> 01:13:55,933
Find it.

1208
01:14:04,232 --> 01:14:05,859
Gravity's Earthnorm.

1209
01:14:06,526 --> 01:14:08,737
O2 levels check,
pressure...

1210
01:14:09,529 --> 01:14:12,366
If anything's wrong the
scanner's not reading it.

1211
01:14:18,205 --> 01:14:20,582
Well, something sure
the hell ain't right.

1212
01:14:23,543 --> 01:14:24,795
This ain't no
little settlement.

1213
01:14:24,878 --> 01:14:27,714
We flew over at least a
dozen cities just as big.

1214
01:14:27,798 --> 01:14:29,967
Why didn't we ever
hear about this?

1215
01:14:30,050 --> 01:14:31,343
(BEEPING)

1216
01:14:32,052 --> 01:14:33,428
Beacon's up ahead.

1217
01:14:56,493 --> 01:14:57,494
Ho.

1218
01:15:17,556 --> 01:15:19,933
No entry wounds,
fractures.

1219
01:15:20,392 --> 01:15:21,601
Poison?

1220
01:15:34,239 --> 01:15:35,866
Got another one.

1221
01:15:41,455 --> 01:15:43,165
They's just
sitting here.

1222
01:15:44,875 --> 01:15:46,126
They didn't crash.

1223
01:15:47,294 --> 01:15:49,588
<i>(MALE ANNOUNCER CHATTERING)</i>

1224
01:16:00,682 --> 01:16:02,225
Kaylee. Don't...

1225
01:16:02,309 --> 01:16:03,560
(SCREAMS)

1226
01:16:07,981 --> 01:16:10,233
How come these ones
are preserved?

1227
01:16:10,776 --> 01:16:12,903
Place must've gone hermetic
when the power blew.

1228
01:16:12,986 --> 01:16:14,112
Sealed them.

1229
01:16:14,196 --> 01:16:15,655
KAYLEE: What are
they doing?

1230
01:16:16,823 --> 01:16:18,742
What's everybody doing?

1231
01:16:18,992 --> 01:16:21,453
There's no unusual
discoloration.

1232
01:16:21,995 --> 01:16:24,706
Nobody's doubled over
or showing signs of pain.

1233
01:16:25,165 --> 01:16:27,501
MAL: There's gasses that
kill painless, right?

1234
01:16:27,751 --> 01:16:30,170
They didn't fall.
None of them.

1235
01:16:30,545 --> 01:16:32,297
They just lay down.

1236
01:16:32,422 --> 01:16:34,341
(RIVER MUTTERING IN CHINESE)

1237
01:16:36,051 --> 01:16:39,304
Make them stop.
They're everywhere.

1238
01:16:40,222 --> 01:16:42,349
Every city, every...

1239
01:16:42,641 --> 01:16:45,519
Every house, every room,
they're all inside me.

1240
01:16:45,644 --> 01:16:49,064
I can hear them all, and
they're saying nothing!

1241
01:16:50,107 --> 01:16:51,108
Get up.

1242
01:16:52,192 --> 01:16:53,693
Please get up.

1243
01:16:54,861 --> 01:16:56,696
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

1244
01:16:58,490 --> 01:17:00,784
Please, God,
make me a stone.

1245
01:17:01,993 --> 01:17:03,829
She is starting
to damage my calm.

1246
01:17:03,912 --> 01:17:05,413
ZOE: Jayne.
She's right!

1247
01:17:06,414 --> 01:17:08,041
Everybody's dead.

1248
01:17:09,543 --> 01:17:11,837
This whole world is
dead for no reason!

1249
01:17:14,256 --> 01:17:16,174
Let's get to
the beacon.

1250
01:17:42,242 --> 01:17:44,161
WASH: This is the source?

1251
01:17:47,497 --> 01:17:49,749
JAYNE: This ship's
banged up all to hell.

1252
01:18:06,975 --> 01:18:09,769
<i>These are just a few of
the images we've recorded.</i>

1253
01:18:10,854 --> 01:18:12,439
<i>And you can see</i>

1254
01:18:14,107 --> 01:18:15,650
<i>it isn't what we thought.</i>

1255
01:18:17,235 --> 01:18:18,737
<i>There's been no war here,</i>

1256
01:18:19,738 --> 01:18:22,824
<i>and no terraforming event.
The environment is stable.</i>

1257
01:18:27,954 --> 01:18:29,372
<i>It's the Pax.</i>

1258
01:18:30,874 --> 01:18:35,212
<i>The G-23 Paxilon Hydroclorate
that we added to the air processors.</i>

1259
01:18:36,171 --> 01:18:39,925
<i>It was supposed to calm the
population, weed out aggression.</i>

1260
01:18:42,010 --> 01:18:43,637
<i>Well, it works.</i>

1261
01:18:44,554 --> 01:18:46,973
<i>The people here
stopped fighting.</i>

1262
01:18:47,974 --> 01:18:50,602
<i>And then they stopped
everything else.</i>

1263
01:18:55,482 --> 01:18:57,692
<i>They stopped going to work,</i>

1264
01:18:58,568 --> 01:19:02,822
<i>they stopped breeding,
talking, eating.</i>

1265
01:19:04,658 --> 01:19:08,912
<i>There's 30 million people here, and
they all just let themselves die.</i>

1266
01:19:09,412 --> 01:19:10,413
<i>(CRASHING)</i>

1267
01:19:10,497 --> 01:19:11,665
<i>(GASPS)</i>

1268
01:19:11,998 --> 01:19:13,416
<i>I have to be quick.</i>

1269
01:19:14,542 --> 01:19:16,211
<i>About a tenth of
a percent of</i>

1270
01:19:16,294 --> 01:19:18,630
<i>the population had the
opposite reaction to the Pax.</i>

1271
01:19:19,256 --> 01:19:22,926
<i>Their aggressor response
increased beyond madness.</i>

1272
01:19:23,343 --> 01:19:24,552
<i>They have become...</i>

1273
01:19:25,011 --> 01:19:26,346
<i>(CRASHING)</i>

1274
01:19:26,930 --> 01:19:28,598
<i>Well, they've killed
most of us.</i>

1275
01:19:29,683 --> 01:19:31,434
<i>And not just killed,</i>

1276
01:19:33,270 --> 01:19:35,021
<i>they've done things.</i>

1277
01:19:35,522 --> 01:19:38,692
Reavers. They
made them.

1278
01:19:40,277 --> 01:19:44,406
<i>I won't live to report this,
but people have to know.</i>

1279
01:19:45,699 --> 01:19:47,492
<i>We meant it
for the best,</i>

1280
01:19:47,993 --> 01:19:49,077
<i>to make people safer.</i>

1281
01:19:49,160 --> 01:19:51,079
<i>(REAVERS GROWLING)</i>

1282
01:19:51,162 --> 01:19:54,207
<i>God!</i>

1283
01:19:55,000 --> 01:19:57,043
<i>(WOMAN SCREAMING)</i>

1284
01:19:57,502 --> 01:19:58,712
<i>(REAVER GROWLING)</i>

1285
01:19:59,045 --> 01:20:00,922
Turn it off.

1286
01:20:05,051 --> 01:20:06,886
(SOBBING)

1287
01:20:20,400 --> 01:20:21,776
(RETCHING)

1288
01:20:25,613 --> 01:20:26,823
River.

1289
01:20:26,906 --> 01:20:28,575
I'm all right.

1290
01:20:36,583 --> 01:20:38,001
I'm all right.

1291
01:20:46,259 --> 01:20:48,720
<i>MAL: This report is
maybe 12 years old.</i>

1292
01:20:49,721 --> 01:20:53,600
Parliament buried it, and it stayed
buried till River dug it up.

1293
01:20:55,226 --> 01:20:57,645
This is what they
feared she knew.

1294
01:20:58,271 --> 01:21:00,106
And they were
right to fear,

1295
01:21:00,648 --> 01:21:03,651
because there's a whole universe of
folk who are gonna know it, too.

1296
01:21:03,735 --> 01:21:05,362
They're gonna see it.

1297
01:21:05,945 --> 01:21:08,615
Somebody has to speak
for these people.

1298
01:21:12,035 --> 01:21:14,371
You all got on this boat
for different reasons,

1299
01:21:14,454 --> 01:21:16,623
but you all come
to the same place.

1300
01:21:17,082 --> 01:21:20,251
So now I'm asking more of
you than I have before.

1301
01:21:21,378 --> 01:21:22,712
Maybe all.

1302
01:21:24,672 --> 01:21:27,884
Sure as I know anything I know
this, they will try again.

1303
01:21:29,260 --> 01:21:31,721
Maybe on another world, maybe on
this very ground swept clean.

1304
01:21:31,805 --> 01:21:34,641
A year from now, 10, they'll
swing back to the belief

1305
01:21:34,808 --> 01:21:36,893
that they can
make people

1306
01:21:39,604 --> 01:21:40,605
better.

1307
01:21:43,775 --> 01:21:45,819
And I do not
hold to that.

1308
01:21:48,154 --> 01:21:49,572
So no more running.

1309
01:21:52,117 --> 01:21:53,827
I aim to misbehave.

1310
01:22:01,626 --> 01:22:03,878
Shepherd Book
used to tell me,

1311
01:22:03,962 --> 01:22:06,005
"if you can't do
something smart,

1312
01:22:07,549 --> 01:22:09,342
do something right."

1313
01:22:10,635 --> 01:22:11,845
Do we have a plan?

1314
01:22:11,928 --> 01:22:13,346
Mr. Universe.

1315
01:22:13,930 --> 01:22:15,932
We haven't the equipment
to broadwave this code,

1316
01:22:16,015 --> 01:22:18,518
but he can put it on every
screen for 30 worlds.

1317
01:22:19,102 --> 01:22:20,854
He's pretty damn close, too.

1318
01:22:21,396 --> 01:22:22,522
We still got
the Reavers

1319
01:22:22,605 --> 01:22:24,858
and probably the Alliance,
between us and him.

1320
01:22:25,150 --> 01:22:27,861
JAYNE: That's two armies
against our one bitty cannon.

1321
01:22:28,027 --> 01:22:31,030
It's a fair bet the Alliance
knows about Mr. Universe.

1322
01:22:31,114 --> 01:22:32,574
They're gonna
see this coming.

1323
01:22:33,700 --> 01:22:34,701
No.

1324
01:22:36,744 --> 01:22:39,080
They're not gonna
see this coming.

1325
01:22:39,706 --> 01:22:42,083
(ENGINE REVVING)

1326
01:22:47,380 --> 01:22:49,299
<i>No problem. Bring it on.
Bring it on. Bring it on.</i>

1327
01:22:49,716 --> 01:22:52,343
<i>From here to the eyes and
ears of the 'verse. That's my motto,</i>

1328
01:22:52,427 --> 01:22:54,804
<i>or it might be, if I
start having a motto.</i>

1329
01:22:54,888 --> 01:22:55,930
We won't be long.

1330
01:22:56,014 --> 01:22:57,974
<i>You're going to get caught
in the ion cloud.</i>

1331
01:22:58,057 --> 01:22:59,684
<i>It'll play merry hob
with your radar,</i>

1332
01:22:59,767 --> 01:23:02,645
<i>but pretty lights and a few miles
after, you'll be right in my orbit.</i>

1333
01:23:02,729 --> 01:23:04,898
You'll let us know if
anyone else comes at you?

1334
01:23:04,981 --> 01:23:06,733
You'll be the first.

1335
01:23:12,780 --> 01:23:13,990
There.

1336
01:23:14,199 --> 01:23:16,242
Toss me my 30 coin, but I
got a news wave for you...

1337
01:23:16,326 --> 01:23:17,619
(GRUNTING)

1338
01:23:26,628 --> 01:23:29,756
Call in every ship in the quadrant.
We'll meet them in the air.

1339
01:23:31,382 --> 01:23:32,926
Destroy it all.

1340
01:23:59,619 --> 01:24:02,038
<i>MAL: Wash, we
almost through?</i>

1341
01:24:24,060 --> 01:24:25,061
<i>Now!</i>

1342
01:24:30,608 --> 01:24:32,277
WASH: Go! Move!

1343
01:24:51,963 --> 01:24:54,007
I'm reading activity
in the cloud.

1344
01:24:54,090 --> 01:24:56,134
Lock and fire
on my command.

1345
01:24:58,261 --> 01:25:00,555
You should have let
me see her, Captain.

1346
01:25:01,681 --> 01:25:05,518
We should have done this as men.
Not with fire.

1347
01:25:05,768 --> 01:25:06,769
<i>HELMSMAN: Sir.</i>

1348
01:25:06,853 --> 01:25:08,563
(ELECTRONIC BEEPING)

1349
01:25:12,275 --> 01:25:14,027
Vessel in range.
Lock on.

1350
01:25:21,951 --> 01:25:23,870
Bastard's not even
changing course.

1351
01:25:29,042 --> 01:25:30,043
Sir!

1352
01:25:33,671 --> 01:25:36,758
Target the Reavers.
Target the Reavers!

1353
01:25:36,841 --> 01:25:39,135
Target everyone!
Somebody fire!

1354
01:25:56,694 --> 01:26:00,990
I am a leaf on the wind.
Watch how I soar.

1355
01:26:15,421 --> 01:26:17,090
Chicken's come
home to roost.

1356
01:26:18,591 --> 01:26:20,677
MAL: The hell?
It's okay.

1357
01:26:20,843 --> 01:26:21,844
I am a leaf on the wind!

1358
01:26:21,928 --> 01:26:23,221
What does that mean?

1359
01:26:27,433 --> 01:26:28,935
We're almost through.

1360
01:26:45,618 --> 01:26:48,037
Yes! Yes! No! No! No!

1361
01:27:04,887 --> 01:27:06,472
(RUMBLING)

1362
01:27:41,007 --> 01:27:42,508
We're not alone.

1363
01:27:49,223 --> 01:27:50,349
EMP!

1364
01:27:51,225 --> 01:27:52,977
Everybody, strap
yourselves into something!

1365
01:27:53,060 --> 01:27:54,061
Jayne.
Got it.

1366
01:27:55,396 --> 01:27:57,148
Kaylee, come on.

1367
01:28:09,911 --> 01:28:11,287
We're fried.
I got no control.

1368
01:28:11,370 --> 01:28:12,538
Where's the backup?

1369
01:28:12,872 --> 01:28:14,916
Where's the backup?

1370
01:28:15,166 --> 01:28:16,876
(GLASS SHATTERING)

1371
01:28:20,129 --> 01:28:21,422
(EXPLOSIONS)

1372
01:28:22,298 --> 01:28:23,674
Check! Check!

1373
01:28:23,758 --> 01:28:25,301
(ENGINE WHINING)

1374
01:28:26,135 --> 01:28:28,137
(JAYNE SCREAMING)

1375
01:28:40,817 --> 01:28:42,652
(WHOOSHING)

1376
01:28:43,528 --> 01:28:44,946
(RUMBLING)

1377
01:28:48,074 --> 01:28:49,200
MAL: Get up!

1378
01:28:49,283 --> 01:28:50,326
KAYLEE: Stop it!

1379
01:28:55,915 --> 01:28:58,000
Backup reads at 20%.
Can you get us down?

1380
01:28:58,084 --> 01:28:59,335
I'm going to have
to glide her in.

1381
01:28:59,418 --> 01:29:01,170
Will that work?

1382
01:29:11,597 --> 01:29:13,516
(SCREAMING)

1383
01:29:43,212 --> 01:29:45,131
(PANTING)

1384
01:29:55,933 --> 01:29:57,643
I am a leaf on the wind.

1385
01:29:59,854 --> 01:30:00,897
Watch how...

1386
01:30:00,980 --> 01:30:02,023
(GASPS)

1387
01:30:03,941 --> 01:30:08,404
Wash, baby. Baby, no. Baby, come on.
You gotta go. Come on.

1388
01:30:08,487 --> 01:30:12,158
We gotta move. Baby, please.
We gotta move, baby, come on.

1389
01:30:15,494 --> 01:30:16,495
MAL: Zoe!

1390
01:30:17,747 --> 01:30:19,665
Move out! Now!

1391
01:30:23,502 --> 01:30:24,545
Go. Go.

1392
01:30:25,212 --> 01:30:26,547
Head inside!

1393
01:30:45,650 --> 01:30:47,234
Jayne, rearguard.

1394
01:30:54,867 --> 01:30:55,826
Zoe, what've we got?

1395
01:30:55,910 --> 01:30:57,036
ZOE: Sir,

1396
01:30:59,038 --> 01:31:00,289
this is a good
hold point.

1397
01:31:00,623 --> 01:31:02,249
We all stay together.
No.

1398
01:31:02,333 --> 01:31:03,501
They have to come
through here.

1399
01:31:03,584 --> 01:31:05,544
They'll bottleneck,
we can thin them out.

1400
01:31:05,628 --> 01:31:08,422
We get pushed back,
there's the blast doors.

1401
01:31:08,547 --> 01:31:10,883
I can rig them so they won't
reopen once they close.

1402
01:31:10,967 --> 01:31:11,968
Shut them and
hide until I get...

1403
01:31:12,051 --> 01:31:14,011
We need to draw
them till it's done.

1404
01:31:15,137 --> 01:31:17,515
This is the place.
We'll buy you the time.

1405
01:31:22,395 --> 01:31:24,814
All right, let's move these
crates back there for cover.

1406
01:31:24,897 --> 01:31:27,233
Make sure they ain't filled
with nothing goes boom.

1407
01:31:27,692 --> 01:31:29,735
Wait, Wash!
Where's Wash?

1408
01:31:30,861 --> 01:31:32,446
He ain't coming.

1409
01:31:37,576 --> 01:31:39,662
Move the gorramn crates!

1410
01:31:52,216 --> 01:31:53,843
(REAVERS HOWLING)

1411
01:31:57,346 --> 01:31:59,849
Tell me you brought
them this time.

1412
01:31:59,974 --> 01:32:01,726
(REAVERS GROWLING)

1413
01:32:08,607 --> 01:32:10,359
(EXPLOSION)

1414
01:32:13,612 --> 01:32:15,197
(GRUNTING)

1415
01:32:22,580 --> 01:32:23,831
Zoe?

1416
01:32:26,000 --> 01:32:27,418
Are you here?

1417
01:32:27,501 --> 01:32:28,627
Do the job, sir.

1418
01:32:31,213 --> 01:32:33,841
You hold. Hold
till I get back.

1419
01:32:37,928 --> 01:32:38,971
Captain's right.

1420
01:32:39,055 --> 01:32:42,058
Can't be thinking on revenge if
we're gonna get through this.

1421
01:32:42,141 --> 01:32:44,769
Do you really think any of us
are gonna get through this?

1422
01:32:48,314 --> 01:32:49,356
I might.

1423
01:33:04,371 --> 01:33:05,998
(STATIC CRACKLING)

1424
01:33:06,415 --> 01:33:07,416
No.

1425
01:33:28,979 --> 01:33:29,980
<i>Mal.</i>

1426
01:33:30,856 --> 01:33:32,566
<i>Guy killed me, Mal.</i>

1427
01:33:32,983 --> 01:33:36,195
<i>He killed me with a sword.
How weird is that?</i>

1428
01:33:37,071 --> 01:33:40,991
<i>I got a short span here.</i>

1429
01:33:42,451 --> 01:33:44,203
<i>They destroyed
my equipment,</i>

1430
01:33:44,537 --> 01:33:46,122
<i>but I have
a backup unit.</i>

1431
01:33:46,205 --> 01:33:48,582
<i>Bottom of the complex,
right over the generator.</i>

1432
01:33:49,041 --> 01:33:52,211
<i>Hard to get to.
I know they missed it.</i>

1433
01:33:53,003 --> 01:33:55,214
<i>They can't stop
the signal, Mal.</i>

1434
01:33:56,090 --> 01:33:58,509
<i>They can never
stop the signal.</i>

1435
01:33:59,885 --> 01:34:01,846
(REAVERS GROWLING)

1436
01:34:02,721 --> 01:34:05,099
The Reavers. They are
all made up of rage.

1437
01:34:05,182 --> 01:34:06,225
It's okay.
It's okay.

1438
01:34:06,267 --> 01:34:07,977
(SHUSHING)
I can't shut them up.

1439
01:34:08,894 --> 01:34:10,604
(BANGING ON DOOR)

1440
01:34:11,730 --> 01:34:12,898
Stay low.

1441
01:34:13,482 --> 01:34:16,944
She picked a sweet bung of a
time to go helpless on us.

1442
01:34:18,112 --> 01:34:19,280
Jayne and I take
the first wave.

1443
01:34:19,363 --> 01:34:21,907
Nobody shoots unless
they get past our fire.

1444
01:34:23,242 --> 01:34:24,743
(BANGING ON DOOR)

1445
01:34:25,703 --> 01:34:28,330
I didn't plan on
going out like this.

1446
01:34:30,166 --> 01:34:32,418
I think we did
right, but...

1447
01:34:33,460 --> 01:34:37,756
No. I never
planned anything.

1448
01:34:39,717 --> 01:34:41,927
I just wanted to
keep River safe.

1449
01:34:45,681 --> 01:34:49,351
Spent so much time on
Serenity ignoring anything

1450
01:34:50,311 --> 01:34:52,813
that I wanted
for myself.

1451
01:34:57,568 --> 01:34:59,945
My one regret
in all of this

1452
01:35:01,238 --> 01:35:02,948
is never being with you.

1453
01:35:05,075 --> 01:35:06,410
With me?

1454
01:35:08,162 --> 01:35:10,164
You mean to say, as...

1455
01:35:12,124 --> 01:35:13,250
Sex?

1456
01:35:15,502 --> 01:35:17,296
I mean to say.

1457
01:35:18,631 --> 01:35:19,965
(METAL SQUEAKS)

1458
01:35:22,259 --> 01:35:25,387
Hell with this.
I'm gonna live.

1459
01:35:39,318 --> 01:35:42,655
<i>Mal. Guy killed me, Mal.</i>

1460
01:35:43,739 --> 01:35:45,407
<i>He killed me with a sword.</i>

1461
01:35:45,991 --> 01:35:47,952
(REAVERS GROWLING)

1462
01:35:54,667 --> 01:35:56,835
(BANGING)

1463
01:36:24,113 --> 01:36:25,698
"Hard to get to."

1464
01:36:27,032 --> 01:36:28,701
That's a fact.

1465
01:36:32,204 --> 01:36:33,622
(GROWLING)

1466
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:37,501
Zoe, gorrammit!

1467
01:36:38,502 --> 01:36:40,713
(REAVERS SHRIEKING)

1468
01:36:46,302 --> 01:36:47,511
(GRUNTING)

1469
01:36:53,350 --> 01:36:55,686
Zoe, get your ass
back on the line!

1470
01:36:56,687 --> 01:36:58,105
(SCREAMS)

1471
01:37:09,575 --> 01:37:10,743
(GROANING)

1472
01:37:12,202 --> 01:37:13,912
You shot me in the back!

1473
01:37:15,539 --> 01:37:18,000
I haven't made you
angry, have I?

1474
01:37:18,083 --> 01:37:21,170
There are a lot of innocent people
in the air being killed right now.

1475
01:37:21,253 --> 01:37:23,714
You have no idea
how true that is.

1476
01:37:25,174 --> 01:37:26,842
I know the secret.

1477
01:37:27,593 --> 01:37:30,054
The truth that burned
up River Tam's brain.

1478
01:37:30,846 --> 01:37:34,933
Rest of the 'verse is going
to know it, too. 'Cause they need to.

1479
01:37:36,810 --> 01:37:39,313
Do you really believe that?

1480
01:37:39,396 --> 01:37:40,522
I do.

1481
01:37:40,606 --> 01:37:42,733
You willing to die
for that belief?

1482
01:37:45,110 --> 01:37:46,278
I am.

1483
01:37:49,948 --> 01:37:51,200
(GRUNTING)

1484
01:37:53,077 --> 01:37:55,120
Of course, that ain't
exactly Plan A.

1485
01:38:01,168 --> 01:38:03,128
(GROANING)

1486
01:38:21,647 --> 01:38:22,689
Spine's intact.

1487
01:38:22,773 --> 01:38:23,941
Just give me a bandage.

1488
01:38:38,831 --> 01:38:39,998
(GRUNTING)

1489
01:39:05,274 --> 01:39:07,192
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1490
01:39:14,658 --> 01:39:15,951
(SOBBING)

1491
01:39:17,536 --> 01:39:18,996
JAYNE: Up high, left!

1492
01:39:23,542 --> 01:39:24,877
(GROANS)

1493
01:39:25,586 --> 01:39:26,628
(GASPS)

1494
01:39:26,712 --> 01:39:28,172
Kaylee!

1495
01:39:28,714 --> 01:39:30,549
(SCREAMING)

1496
01:39:36,638 --> 01:39:38,056
(GROANS)

1497
01:39:40,851 --> 01:39:44,771
Fall back! Everybody, fall back!
Fall back now!

1498
01:39:54,364 --> 01:39:55,657
Jayne, grenade.

1499
01:39:57,034 --> 01:39:59,244
Very last one.

1500
01:40:05,250 --> 01:40:06,335
They're gonna get in.

1501
01:40:06,710 --> 01:40:09,421
I can close it
from the outside.

1502
01:40:09,796 --> 01:40:11,798
No one's coming
back from that.

1503
01:40:14,760 --> 01:40:16,720
How much ammo
do we have?

1504
01:40:16,845 --> 01:40:20,682
Three, four max,
and my swinging cod. That's all.

1505
01:40:20,766 --> 01:40:21,808
The lift isn't moving.

1506
01:40:21,892 --> 01:40:24,353
When they come, try to
plug the hole with it.

1507
01:40:24,436 --> 01:40:26,855
I'm starting to lose
some feeling here.

1508
01:40:26,939 --> 01:40:29,650
Lie still. I'm going
to give you something...

1509
01:40:31,652 --> 01:40:32,653
My bag.

1510
01:40:32,819 --> 01:40:33,946
(GUN FIRES)

1511
01:40:37,157 --> 01:40:38,909
(GUN FIRING)

1512
01:40:42,996 --> 01:40:44,540
Keep pressure here.

1513
01:40:46,291 --> 01:40:47,292
SIMON: My bag.

1514
01:40:47,793 --> 01:40:48,794
I need

1515
01:40:49,628 --> 01:40:53,131
adrenaline and a shot of

1516
01:40:53,632 --> 01:40:55,259
calaphar for Kaylee.

1517
01:40:57,970 --> 01:40:59,638
I can't.

1518
01:41:03,475 --> 01:41:04,476
River.

1519
01:41:09,606 --> 01:41:11,441
River, I'm sorry.

1520
01:41:11,525 --> 01:41:12,526
No.

1521
01:41:13,652 --> 01:41:14,903
No.

1522
01:41:21,994 --> 01:41:23,078
I hate to leave.

1523
01:41:23,161 --> 01:41:24,204
You won't.

1524
01:41:27,124 --> 01:41:29,710
You take care
of me, Simon.

1525
01:41:32,838 --> 01:41:35,465
You've always
taken care of me.

1526
01:41:40,804 --> 01:41:41,805
My turn.

1527
01:41:47,144 --> 01:41:48,687
(GRUNTING)

1528
01:41:59,573 --> 01:42:01,867
(OPERATIVE AND MAL GRUNTING)

1529
01:42:36,818 --> 01:42:39,446
Do you know what
your sin is, Mal?

1530
01:42:40,072 --> 01:42:43,408
Hell. I'm a fan
of all seven.

1531
01:42:43,742 --> 01:42:45,327
(GRUNTING)

1532
01:42:49,915 --> 01:42:51,667
But right now,

1533
01:42:52,751 --> 01:42:54,753
I'm going to have
to go with wrath.

1534
01:42:59,216 --> 01:43:01,677
We ain't got long.

1535
01:43:03,887 --> 01:43:05,764
(THUDDING)

1536
01:43:07,683 --> 01:43:09,601
You suppose he
got through?

1537
01:43:10,852 --> 01:43:12,813
Do you think Mal
got the word out?

1538
01:43:13,480 --> 01:43:17,901
He got through. I
know he got through.

1539
01:43:19,027 --> 01:43:20,362
(GROANS)

1540
01:43:20,445 --> 01:43:21,822
(COUGHS)

1541
01:43:29,162 --> 01:43:30,622
(GROANS)
I'm sorry.

1542
01:43:33,458 --> 01:43:36,253
You should know there's
no shame in this.

1543
01:43:38,463 --> 01:43:40,590
You've done
remarkable things.

1544
01:43:41,800 --> 01:43:44,010
But you're
fighting a war

1545
01:43:45,178 --> 01:43:46,388
you've already lost.

1546
01:43:47,222 --> 01:43:48,348
(GROANS)

1547
01:43:50,142 --> 01:43:51,351
(GASPING)

1548
01:43:51,435 --> 01:43:53,145
Well, I'm known for that.

1549
01:43:54,312 --> 01:43:55,605
(GROANING)

1550
01:44:02,028 --> 01:44:05,657
Piece of shrapnel tore up that
nerve cluster my first tour.

1551
01:44:06,283 --> 01:44:07,617
Had it moved.

1552
01:44:09,202 --> 01:44:10,662
Sorry about the throat.

1553
01:44:11,246 --> 01:44:14,082
Expect you'd want to say your
famous last words right now.

1554
01:44:15,167 --> 01:44:16,710
Just one trouble.

1555
01:44:21,423 --> 01:44:22,924
I ain't gonna kill you.

1556
01:44:23,592 --> 01:44:25,010
(GASPING)

1557
01:44:26,428 --> 01:44:29,514
Hell, I'm gonna grant
your greatest wish.

1558
01:44:30,015 --> 01:44:32,225
(BEEPING)

1559
01:44:36,855 --> 01:44:39,691
I'm gonna show you
a world without sin.

1560
01:44:45,530 --> 01:44:47,574
<i>These are just a few of the
few images we've recorded.</i>

1561
01:44:47,657 --> 01:44:48,700
<i>And you can see</i>

1562
01:44:51,620 --> 01:44:53,789
<i>it isn't what we thought.</i>

1563
01:44:55,415 --> 01:44:57,292
<i>There's been no war here,</i>

1564
01:44:58,043 --> 01:45:02,339
<i>and no terraforming event.
The environment is stable.</i>

1565
01:45:03,882 --> 01:45:05,675
<i>It's the Pax.</i>

1566
01:45:07,385 --> 01:45:11,723
<i>The G-23 Paxilon Hydroclorate
that we added to the air processors.</i>

1567
01:45:12,432 --> 01:45:15,060
<i>It was supposed to
calm the population...</i>

1568
01:45:15,268 --> 01:45:17,020
(ROARING)

1569
01:45:43,630 --> 01:45:45,298
<i>We meant it for the best,</i>

1570
01:45:46,216 --> 01:45:47,759
<i>to make people safer.</i>

1571
01:45:47,843 --> 01:45:49,469
<i>(REAVERS GROWLING)</i>

1572
01:45:49,553 --> 01:45:50,846
<i>God!</i>

1573
01:45:51,596 --> 01:45:52,764
<i>(REAVERS GROWLING)</i>

1574
01:45:52,848 --> 01:45:55,141
<i>(WOMAN SCREAMING)</i>

1575
01:46:06,611 --> 01:46:08,446
(PANTING)

1576
01:46:13,702 --> 01:46:15,036
Sir?

1577
01:46:15,120 --> 01:46:16,162
It's done.

1578
01:46:19,374 --> 01:46:20,709
Report.

1579
01:46:22,836 --> 01:46:24,004
River?

1580
01:46:27,799 --> 01:46:29,050
(CLANKING)

1581
01:46:49,571 --> 01:46:50,572
SOLDIER 1: Drop your weapons!

1582
01:46:50,655 --> 01:46:51,698
SOLDIER 2: Do it now.

1583
01:46:51,781 --> 01:46:53,158
Weapons down.
Let it down, now.

1584
01:46:53,241 --> 01:46:54,826
I want to see your
hands in the air.

1585
01:46:54,910 --> 01:46:56,786
Stand down.
Do it.

1586
01:47:02,208 --> 01:47:03,710
Targets are acquired.

1587
01:47:03,793 --> 01:47:05,170
<i>Do we have a kill order?</i>

1588
01:47:08,173 --> 01:47:09,966
<i>Do we have an order?</i>

1589
01:47:18,099 --> 01:47:19,351
<i>THE OPERATIVE: Stand down.</i>

1590
01:47:20,477 --> 01:47:23,229
<i>Stand down. It's finished.</i>

1591
01:47:27,067 --> 01:47:28,443
<i>We're finished.</i>

1592
01:49:30,815 --> 01:49:32,650
THE OPERATIVE: It's
not over, you know.

1593
01:49:34,319 --> 01:49:37,030
I can't guarantee that
they won't come after you.

1594
01:49:37,864 --> 01:49:38,865
The Parliament.

1595
01:49:39,824 --> 01:49:42,744
Your broadwave about Miranda
has weakened their regime.

1596
01:49:42,827 --> 01:49:47,207
They are not gone and
they are not forgiving.

1597
01:49:47,791 --> 01:49:50,251
That don't bode
especially well for you,

1598
01:49:50,960 --> 01:49:54,005
giving the order to let us
go, patching up our hurt.

1599
01:49:55,381 --> 01:49:58,843
I told them the Tams were no
longer a threat, damage done.

1600
01:49:59,344 --> 01:50:00,845
They might listen,

1601
01:50:01,679 --> 01:50:05,058
but I think they know
I'm no longer their man.

1602
01:50:06,810 --> 01:50:09,896
They take you down, I don't
expect to grieve over much.

1603
01:50:12,190 --> 01:50:14,609
Like to kill you myself,
I see you again.

1604
01:50:15,401 --> 01:50:16,402
You won't.

1605
01:50:19,322 --> 01:50:21,533
There is nothing
left to see.

1606
01:50:27,205 --> 01:50:28,748
Sir, we have
a green light.

1607
01:50:29,207 --> 01:50:31,417
Inspection's pos and we're
clear for up-thrust.

1608
01:50:37,882 --> 01:50:40,009
Think she'll
hold together?

1609
01:50:41,010 --> 01:50:43,638
She's tore up plenty.
But she'll fly true.

1610
01:50:47,976 --> 01:50:50,228
Make sure
everything's secure.

1611
01:50:52,063 --> 01:50:53,648
Could be bumpy.

1612
01:50:53,731 --> 01:50:54,983
Always is.

1613
01:51:02,407 --> 01:51:03,366
Taking her out.

1614
01:51:03,449 --> 01:51:05,994
Should be about a day's ride
to get you back to your girls.

1615
01:51:06,077 --> 01:51:07,245
Right.

1616
01:51:08,663 --> 01:51:10,874
Ready to get off this heap,
back to civilized life?

1617
01:51:10,957 --> 01:51:12,083
I...

1618
01:51:16,754 --> 01:51:18,089
I don't know.

1619
01:51:20,133 --> 01:51:21,301
Good answer.

1620
01:51:46,492 --> 01:51:49,078
So you gonna ride shotgun
with me, help me fly?

1621
01:51:49,287 --> 01:51:50,538
That's the plan.

1622
01:51:51,206 --> 01:51:52,665
Think you can
work out...

1623
01:51:52,749 --> 01:51:54,250
(ENGINE REVVING)

1624
01:52:00,423 --> 01:52:01,424
Okay.

1625
01:52:02,800 --> 01:52:05,929
Clearly some aptitude
for the...

1626
01:52:07,430 --> 01:52:09,974
it ain't all buttons and
charts, little albatross.

1627
01:52:10,391 --> 01:52:12,518
You know what the first
rule of flying is?

1628
01:52:13,019 --> 01:52:16,022
Well, I suppose you do, since you
already know what I'm about to say.

1629
01:52:17,065 --> 01:52:18,524
I do.

1630
01:52:19,692 --> 01:52:21,444
But I like to
hear you say it.

1631
01:52:26,199 --> 01:52:27,242
Love.

1632
01:52:27,575 --> 01:52:29,452
You can learn all the
math in the 'verse,

1633
01:52:29,535 --> 01:52:31,579
but you take a boat in the
air that you don't love,

1634
01:52:31,663 --> 01:52:34,499
she'll shake you off just as
sure as the turn of the worlds.

1635
01:52:37,835 --> 01:52:40,546
Love keeps her in the air
when she ought to fall down,

1636
01:52:42,006 --> 01:52:44,342
tells you she's hurting
before she keels.

1637
01:52:47,136 --> 01:52:48,346
Makes her a home.

1638
01:52:49,514 --> 01:52:51,099
(RAIN PATTERING)

1639
01:52:53,977 --> 01:52:55,853
Storm's getting worse.

1640
01:52:58,147 --> 01:53:00,858
We'll pass through
it soon enough.

1641
01:53:05,697 --> 01:53:07,115
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

1642
01:53:21,921 --> 01:53:22,964
<i>MAL: What was that?</i>